SOAPBOX: Conditions were much better that I had pesimistically anticipated.
SOAPBOX: Started S&P on 10m and rapidly changed to run when observed a lot of JAs on the band.
SOAPBOX: 30 minutes later I switched to 15M where I had decent run to AS , Greatly surprised to being called by a VK9DX and some other -hard to reach- entities.
SOAPBOX: 40M and 80M and 160 were useless due to the brutal urban noise.
SOAPBOX: Saturdary XE sunrise (13.00z) morning presented with a nice EU opening.
SOAPBOX: 2nd day was also great nice multipliers being present on the band.
SOAPBOX: Nice stateside run on the last 2 hours , closing the last minutes of the test hunting for the mults available
SOAPBOX: Enjoyed a lot this test and thanks for the Qs
